PERMITTED PURPOSES

For each of the purposes below, you may do with the software everything that
purpose reasonably requires, including reproducing it, changing it, creating
works based on it, compiling, installing, running, and testing it and any
changed version, and making whatever local adjustments building or running it
on your own machine requires, such as substituting your own code-signing
identity. The purposes are:

(a) Personal use — using the software yourself, for any purpose the license
    below permits.

(b) Auditing — examining, reviewing, testing, and verifying the behavior,
    security, and privacy properties of the software. This purpose applies
    whether you are an individual, a business, or any other commercial
    organization, and whether or not you are paid to perform the audit.

(c) Contributing — preparing and submitting a contribution to the official
    Show KeyPress repository at https://github.com/xkelxmc/keypress-macos.
    For this purpose only, you may also publish the software and your changed
    version of it on the code-hosting service where the official repository is
    hosted, using that service's own contribution functionality: forking the
    repository, pushing branches to your fork, and opening a pull request.

WHAT THESE PERMISSIONS DO NOT ALLOW

None of them lets you:

  - distribute the software, or a changed version of it, anywhere other than
    a fork published under purpose (c);

  - publish or make available a changed version for anyone else to use as
    software;

  - except as an audit under purpose (b) reasonably requires, deploy or use
    the software, or a changed version, as a working tool in a business, or
    for any other commercial purpose. Auditing under purpose (b) is not such a
    use, even when you are a business and even when you are paid to do it;
    running the software to do a business's actual work is such a use, however
    it is described;

  - offer the software or a changed version under any other license terms; or

  - remove or alter this file, the copyright notice, or NOTICE.md in any copy
    you publish, except as part of a contribution you are submitting.

Any copy or changed version you publish under purpose (c) remains subject to
these same terms, including these limitations. Submitting a contribution is
additionally subject to CONTRIBUTING.md.

DURATION

A fork or branch published under purpose (c) is permitted only while it serves
that purpose. Once your contribution is merged, closed, or rejected, once you
stop working on it, or if you do not open a pull request within 90 days of
publishing the fork, you must delete it within 30 days of that happening;
permission to keep it published continues until you delete it or those 30 days
pass, whichever comes first.

The licensor may end these permissions for you by written notice. For copies
already published under them, permission continues until you take them down or
32 days pass, whichever comes first, and you must take them down within those
32 days.

